:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0098 [T9000](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0098) is a backdoor that is a newer variant of the T5000 malware family, also known as Plat1. Its primary function is to gather information about"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s0430", "source": "mitre", "title": "S0430 Winnti for Linux", "tags": ["s0430", "software", "winnti for linux"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S0430 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0430 [Winnti for Linux](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0430) is a trojan, seen since at least 2015, designed specifically for targeting Linux systems. Reporting indicates the winnti malware"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1113", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1113 RAPIDPULSE", "tags": ["rapidpulse", "s1113", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1113 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1113 [RAPIDPULSE](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1113) is a web shell that exists as a modification to a legitimate Pulse Secure file that has been used by [APT5](https://attack.mitre.org/g"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s0032", "source": "mitre", "title": "S0032 gh0st RAT", "tags": ["gh0st rat", "s0032", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S0032 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0032 [gh0st RAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0032) is a remote access tool (RAT). The source code is public and it has been used by multiple groups.(Citation: FireEye Hacking Team)(Citat"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s0140", "source": "mitre", "title": "S0140 Shamoon", "tags": ["s0140", "shamoon", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S0140 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0140 [Shamoon](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0140) is wiper malware that was first used by an Iranian group known as the \"Cutting Sword of Justice\" in 2012. Other versions known as Shamoon"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s0007", "source": "mitre", "title": "S0007 Skeleton Key", "tags": ["s0007", "skeleton key", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S0007 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0007 [Skeleton Key](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0007) is malware used to inject false credentials into domain controllers with the intent of creating a backdoor password. (Citation: Dell"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1021", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1021 DnsSystem", "tags": ["dnssystem", "s1021", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1021 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1021 [DnsSystem](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1021) is a .NET based DNS backdoor, which is a customized version of the open source tool DIG.net, that has been used by [HEXANE](https://att"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s0553", "source": "mitre", "title": "S0553 MoleNet", "tags": ["molenet", "s0553", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S0553 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0553 [MoleNet](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0553) is a downloader tool with backdoor capabilities that has been observed in use since at least 2019.(Citation: Cybereason Molerats Dec 2020"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s0212", "source": "mitre", "title": "S0212 CORALDECK", "tags": ["coraldeck", "s0212", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S0212 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0212 [CORALDECK](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0212) is an exfiltration tool used by [APT37](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0067). (Citation: FireEye APT37 Feb 2018) ## Techniques used -"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s0044", "source": "mitre", "title": "S0044 JHUHUGIT", "tags": ["jhuhugit", "s0044", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK