3 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0803 Data Loss Prevention (DLP) technologies can be used to help identify adversarial attempts to exfiltrate operational information, such as engineering plans, trade secrets, recipes, intellectual property, or process telemet"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0801", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0801 Access Management", "tags": ["access management", "m0801", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0801 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0801 Access Management technologies can be used to enforce authorization polices and decisions, especially when existing field devices do not provide sufficient capabilities to support user identification and authentication. ("}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0816", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0816 Mitigation Limited or Not Effective", "tags": ["m0816", "mitigation", "mitigation limited or not effective"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0816 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0816 This type of attack technique cannot be easily mitigated with preventative controls since it is based on the abuse of system features."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0950", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0950 Exploit Protection", "tags": ["exploit protection", "m0950", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0950 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0950 Use capabilities to detect and block conditions that may lead to or be indicative of a software exploit occurring."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0935", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0935 Limit Access to Resource Over Network", "tags": ["limit access to resource over network", "m0935", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0935 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0935 Prevent access to file shares, remote access to systems, unnecessary services. Mechanisms to limit access may include use of network concentrators, RDP gateways, etc."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0938", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0938 Execution Prevention", "tags": ["execution prevention", "m0938", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0938 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0938 Block execution of code on a system through application control, and/or script blocking."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0814", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0814 Static Network Configuration", "tags": ["m0814", "mitigation", "static network configuration"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0814 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0814 Configure hosts and devices to use static network configurations when possible, protocols that require dynamic discovery/addressing (e.g., ARP, DHCP, DNS) can be used to manipulate network message forwarding and enable va"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0927", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0927 Password Policies", "tags": ["m0927", "mitigation", "password policies"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0927 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0927 Set and enforce secure password policies for accounts."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0926", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0926 Privileged Account Management", "tags": ["m0926", "mitigation", "privileged account management"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0926 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0926 Manage the creation, modification, use, and permissions associated to privileged accounts, including SYSTEM and root."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0804", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0804 Human User Authentication", "tags": ["human user authentication", "m0804", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0804 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0804 Require user authentication before allowing access to data or accepting commands to a device. While strong multi-factor authentication is preferable, it is not always feasible within ICS environments. Performing strong us"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0920", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0920 SSL/TLS Inspection", "tags": ["m0920", "mitigation", "ssl/tls inspection