s any guidance or training given to developers of applications to avoid introducing security weaknesses that an adversary may be able to take advantage of."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0946", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0946 Boot Integrity", "tags": ["boot integrity", "m0946", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0946 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0946 Use secure methods to boot a system and verify the integrity of the operating system and loading mechanisms."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0805", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0805 Mechanical Protection Layers", "tags": ["m0805", "mechanical protection layers", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0805 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0805 Utilize a layered protection design based on physical or mechanical protection systems to prevent damage to property, equipment, human safety, or the environment. Examples include interlocks, rupture disk, release values,"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0951", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0951 Update Software", "tags": ["m0951", "mitigation", "update software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0951 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0951 Perform regular software updates to mitigate exploitation risk. Software updates may need to be scheduled around operational down times."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0815", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0815 Watchdog Timers", "tags": ["m0815", "mitigation", "watchdog timers"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0815 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0815 Utilize watchdog timers to ensure devices can quickly detect whether a system is unresponsive."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0809", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0809 Operational Information Confidentiality", "tags": ["m0809", "mitigation", "operational information confidentiality"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0809 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0809 Deploy mechanisms to protect the confidentiality of information related to operational processes, facility locations, device configurations, programs, or databases that may have information that can be used to infer organ"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0928", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0928 Operating System Configuration", "tags": ["m0928", "mitigation", "operating system configuration"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0928 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0928 Make configuration changes related to the operating system or a common feature of the operating system that result in system hardening against techniques."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0934", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0934 Limit Hardware Installation", "tags": ["limit hardware installation", "m0934", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0934 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0934 Block users or groups from installing or using unapproved hardware on systems, including USB devices."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0941", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0941 Encrypt Sensitive Information", "tags": ["encrypt sensitive information", "m0941", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0941 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0941 Protect sensitive data-at-rest with strong encryption."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0807", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0807 Network Allowlists", "tags": ["m0807", "mitigation", "network allowlists"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0807 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0807 Network allowlists can be implemented through either host-based files or system hosts files to specify what connections (e.g., IP address, MAC address, port, protocol) can be made from a device. Allowlist techniques that "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0817", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0817 Supply Chain Management", "tags": ["m0817", "mitigation", "supply chain management"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0817 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0817 Implement a supply chain management program, including policies and procedures to ensure all devices and components originate from a trusted supplier and are tested to verify their integrity."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0953", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0953 Data Backup", "tags": ["data backup", "m0953", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0953 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0953 Take and store data backups from end user systems and critical servers. Ensure backup and storage systems are hardened and kept separate from the corporate network to prevent compromise. Maintain and exercise incident res"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0810", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0810 Out-of-Band Communications Channel", "tags": ["m0810", "mitigation", "out-of-band communications channel"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0810 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0810 Have alternative methods to support communication requirements during communication failures and data integrity attacks. (Citation: National Institute of Standards and Technology April 2013) (Citation: Defense Advanced Re"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0947", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0947 Audit", "tags": ["audit", "m0947", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0947 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0947 Perform audits or scans of systems, permissions, insecure software, insecure configurations, etc. to identify potential weaknesses. Perform periodic integrity checks of the device to validate the correctness of the firmwa"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0802", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0802 Communication Authenticity", "tags": ["communication authenticity", "m0802", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0802 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0802 When communicating over an untrusted network, utilize secure network protocols that both authenticate the message sender and can verify its integrity. This can be done either through message authentication codes (MACs) or"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0942", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0942 Disable or Remove Feature or Program", "tags": ["disable or remove feature or program", "m0942", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0942 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0942 Remove or deny access to unnecessary and potentially vulnerable software to prevent abuse by adversaries."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0919", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0919 Threat Intelligence Program", "tags": ["m0919", "mitigation", "threat intelligence program"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0919 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0919 A threat intelligence program helps an organization generate their own threat intelligence information and track trends to inform defensive priorities to mitigate risk."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0812", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0812 Safety Instrumented Systems", "tags": ["m0812", "mitigation", "safety instrumented systems"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0812 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0812 Utilize Safety Instrumented Systems (SIS) to provide an additional layer of protection to hazard scenarios that may cause property damage. A SIS will typically include sensors, logic solvers, and a final control element t"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0917", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0917 User Training", "tags": ["m0917", "mitigation", "user training"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0917 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0917 Train users to be aware of access or manipulation attempts by an adversary to reduce the risk of successful spearphishing, social engineering, and other techniques that involve user interaction."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0932", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0932 Multi-factor Authentication", "tags": ["m0932", "mitigation", "multi-factor authentication"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0932 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0932 Use two or more pieces of evidence to authenticate to a system; such as username and password in addition to a token from a physical smart card or token generator. Within industrial control environments assets such as low"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0916", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0916 Vulnerability Scanning", "tags": ["m0916", "mitigation", "vulnerability scanning"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0916 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0916 Vulnerability scanning is used to find potentially exploitable software vulnerabilities to remediate them."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0800", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0800 Authorization Enforcement", "tags": ["authorization enforcement", "m0800", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0800 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0800 The device or system should restrict read, manipulate, or execute privileges to only authenticated users who require access based on approved security policies. Role-based Access Control (RBAC) schemes can help reduce the"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0918", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0918 User Account Management", "tags": ["m0918", "mitigation", "user account management"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0918 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0918 Manage the creation, modification, use, and permissions associated to user accounts."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0811", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0811 Redundancy of Service", "tags": ["m0811", "mitigation", "redundancy of service"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0811 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0811 Redundancy could be provided for both critical ICS devices and services, such as back-up devices or hot-standbys."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0922", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0922 Restrict File and Directory Permissions", "tags": ["m0922", "mitigation", "restrict file and directory permissions"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0922 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0922 Restrict access by setting directory and file permissions that are not specific to users or privileged accounts."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0954", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0954 Software Configuration", "tags": ["m0954", "mitigation", "software configuration"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0954 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0954 Implement configuration changes to software (other than the operating system) to mitigate security risks associated with how the software operates."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0949", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0949 Antivirus/Antimalware", "tags": ["antivirus/antimalware", "m0949", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0949 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0949 Use signatures or heuristics to detect malicious software. Within industrial control environments, antivirus/antimalware installations should be limited to assets that are not involved in critical or real-time operations."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M0806", "source": "mitre", "title": "M0806 Minimize Wireless Signal Propagation", "tags": ["m0806", "minimize wireless signal propagation", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M0806 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M0806 Wireless signals frequently propagate outside of organizational boundaries, which provide opportunities for adversaries to monitor or gain unauthorized access to the wireless network. (Citation: CISA March 2010) To minimi"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-M1061", "source": "mitre", "title": "M1061 Limit Software/Package Installation", "tags": ["limit software/package installation", "m1061", "mitigation"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** M1061 **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/mitigations/M1061 Prevent unauthorized installation of software on ICS assets."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1004", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1004 Industroyer", "tags": ["industroyer", "s1004", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1004 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0001 [Industroyer](https://collaborat