 "tags": ["killdisk", "s1005", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1005 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0016 In 2015 the BlackEnergy malware contained a component called KillDisk. KillDisk's main functionality is to overwrite files with random data, rendering the OS unboo"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1009", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1009 Triton", "tags": ["s1009", "software", "triton"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1009 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1009 [Triton](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1009) is an attack framework built to interact with Triconex Safety Instrumented System (SIS) controllers.(Citation: Blake Johnson, Dan Caban, M"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1002", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1002 BlackEnergy 3", "tags": ["blackenergy 3", "s1002", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1002 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0004 [BlackEnergy 3](https://collaborate.mitre.org/attackics/index.php/Software/S0004) is a malware toolkit that has been used by both criminal and APT actors. It suppo"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1157", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1157 Fuxnet", "tags": ["fuxnet", "s1157", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1157 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1157 [Fuxnet](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1157) is malware designed to impact the industrial network infrastructure managing control system sensors for utility operations in Moscow. [Fux"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1000", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1000 ACAD/Medre.A", "tags": ["acad/medre.a", "s1000", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1000 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1000 [ACAD/Medre.A](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1000) is a worm that steals operational information. The worm collects AutoCAD files with drawings. [ACAD/Medre.A](https://attack.mitre.or"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1165", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1165 FrostyGoop", "tags": ["frostygoop", "s1165", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1165 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1165 [FrostyGoop](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1165) is a Windows-based binary written in Golang that allows for interaction with industrial control system (ICS) equipment via Modbus TCP "}, {"id": "mitre-attack-software-s1045", "source": "mitre", "title": "S1045 INCONTROLLER", "tags": ["incontroller", "s1045", "software"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** S1045 **Type:** software **Aliases:** n/a **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1045 [INCONTROLLER](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1045) is custom malware that includes multiple modules tailored towards ICS devices and technologies, including Schneider Electric and Omr"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-group-g1000", "source": "mitre", "title": "G1000 ALLANITE", "tags": ["allanite", "g1000", "group", "palmetto fusion"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** G1000 **Type:** group **Aliases:** ALLANITE, Palmetto Fusion **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1000 [ALLANITE](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1000) is a suspected Russian cyber espionage group, that has primarily targeted the electric utility sector within the United S"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-group-g1027", "source": "mitre", "title": "G1027 CyberAv3ngers", "tags": ["cyberav3ngers", "g1027", "group", "soldiers of soloman"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** G1027 **Type:** group **Aliases:** CyberAv3ngers, Soldiers of Soloman **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1027 The [CyberAv3ngers](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1027) are a suspected Iranian Government Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC)-affiliated APT group. The ["}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0009", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0009 Oldsmar Treatment Plant Intrusion", "tags": ["c0009", "campaign", "oldsmar treatment plant intrusion"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0009 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Oldsmar Treatment Plant Intrusion **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0009 [Oldsmar Treatment Plant Intrusion](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0009) was a cyber incident involving a water treatment facility in Florida. During th"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0020", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0020 Maroochy Water Breach", "tags": ["c0020", "campaign", "maroochy water breach"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0020 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Maroochy Water Breach **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0020 [Maroochy Water Breach](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0020) was an incident in 2000 where an adversary leveraged the local government’s wastewater control system a"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0031", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0031 Unitronics Defacement Campaign", "tags": ["c0031", "campaign", "unitronics defacement campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0031 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** Unitronics Defacement Campaign **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0031 The [Unitronics Defacement Campaign](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0031) was a collection of intrusions across multiple sectors by the [CyberAv3ngers](htt"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-campaign-c0066", "source": "mitre", "title": "C0066 2026 U.S. Water Utilities Attacks", "tags": ["2026 u.s. water utilities attacks", "2026 water utilities attacks", "c0066", "campaign"], "summary": "**ATT&CK ID:** C0066 **Type:** campaign **Aliases:** 2026 U.S. Water Utilities Attacks, 2026 Water Utilities Attacks **Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0066 [2026 U.S. Water Utilities Attacks](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0066) was a campaign against more than 30 municipal wat"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-process-event-alarm", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Process/Event Alarm", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "process/event alarm"], "summary": "This includes a list of any process alarms or alerts produced to indicate unusual or concerning activity within the operational process (e.g., increased temperature/pressure)"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-software", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Software", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "software"], "summary": "This includes sources of current and expected software or application programs deployed to a device, along with information on the version and patch level for vendor products, full source code for any application programs, and unique identifiers (e.g., hashes, signatures)."}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-process-history-live-data", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Process History/Live Data", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "process history/live data"], "summary": "This includes any data stores that maintain historical or real-time events and telemetry recorded from various sensors or devices"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-device-alarm", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Device Alarm", "tags": ["data-component", "detection", "device alarm"], "summary": "This includes alarms associated with unexpected device functions, such as shutdowns, restarts, failures, or configuration changes"}, {"id": "mitre-attack-datacomponent-asset-inventory", "source": "mitre", "title": "Data Component: Asset Inventory", "tags": ["asset inventory", "data-component", "detection"], "summary": "This includes sources of current and expected devices on the network, including the manufacturer, model, and necessary identifiers (e.g., IP and hardware addresses)"}, {"id": "owasp-cheatsheet-ai-powered-advertising-systems-security-cheat-sheet", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Cheat Sheet: AI-Powered Advertising Systems Security Cheat Sheet", "tags": ["ai-powered advertising syste