tion format for a stack-based virtual machine. Wasm is designed as a portable compilation"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-01-webassembly-reconnaissance", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 01-WebAssembly Reconnaissance", "tags": ["01-webassembly reconnaissance", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# WebAssembly Reconnaissance |ID | |------------| |WSTG-WASM-01| ## Summary WebAssembly (Wasm) is a binary instruction format delivered to the browser as a compiled module. Because it is not human-rea"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-02-webassembly-static-analysis", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 02-WebAssembly Static Analysis", "tags": ["02-webassembly static analysis", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# WebAssembly Static Analysis |ID | |------------| |WSTG-WASM-02| ## Summary Static analysis examines a WebAssembly (Wasm) module without executing it. A Wasm binary has a defined structure made up of"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-03-webassembly-dynamic-analysis", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 03-WebAssembly Dynamic Analysis", "tags": ["03-webassembly dynamic analysis", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# WebAssembly Dynamic Analysis |ID | |------------| |WSTG-WASM-03| ## Summary Dynamic analysis evaluates a WebAssembly (Wasm) module by executing it within its host runtime (primarily modern web brows"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-01-reporting-structure", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 01-Reporting Structure", "tags": ["01-reporting structure", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# Reporting Structure Performing the technical side of the assessment is only half of the overall assessment process. The final product is the production of a well written and informative report. A re"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-02-naming-schemes", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: 02-Naming Schemes", "tags": ["02-naming schemes", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# Vulnerability Naming Schemes With a constantly growing number of IT assets to administer, security practitioners require new and more powerful tools to perform automated and large scale analysis. Th"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-a-history", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: A-History", "tags": ["a-history", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# A. History The Testing Guide v4 was released in 2014. The Testing guide originated in 2003 with Dan Cuthbert as one of the original editors. It was handed over to Eoin Keary in 2005 and transformed "}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-b-testing-tools-resource", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: B-Testing Tools Resource", "tags": ["b-testing tools resource", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# B. Testing Tools Resource ## Introduction This appendix is intended to provide a list of common tools that are used for web application testing. It does not aim to be a complete tool reference, and "}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-c-suggested-reading", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: C-Suggested Reading", "tags": ["c-suggested reading", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# C. Suggested Reading ## Whitepapers - [The Economic Impacts of Inadequate Infrastructure for Software Testing](https://www.nist.gov/system/files/documents/director/planning/report02-3.pdf) - [NIST P"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-d-fuzzing", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: D-Fuzzing", "tags": ["d-fuzzing", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# D. Fuzzing {#fuzzing} ## Introduction Fuzzing is the process or technique of sending a number of request to as target site in a certain interval of time. In other words, it is also similar to brutef"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-e-encoded-injection", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: E-Encoded Injection", "tags": ["e-encoded injection", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# E. Encoded Injection {#encoded-injection} ## Background Character encoding is the process of mapping characters, numbers and other symbols to a standard format. Typically, this is done to create a m"}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-f-leveraging-dev-tools", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: F-Leveraging Dev Tools", "tags": ["f-leveraging dev tools", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# F. Leveraging Dev Tools {#leveraging-dev-tools} This appendix outlines various details for use of in browser Developer Tool functionality to aid in security testing activities. Obviously in browser "}, {"id": "owasp-wstg-g-penetration-testing-methodologies", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP WSTG: G-Penetration Testing Methodologies", "tags": ["g-penetration testing methodologies", "owasp", "testing", "wstg"], "summary": "# G. Penetration Testing Methodologies This appendix documents established penetration testing methodologies and frameworks. These standards provide detailed guidance on testing procedures, phases, an"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-0x00-2021-notice", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: 0x00 2021-notice", "tags": ["0x00 2021-notice", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": " # 發表版本 於 2021 年 9 月 24 日正式發表 ## 專案領袖 - [Andrew van der Stock](mailto:vanderaj@owasp.org) (twitter: [@vanderaj](https://x.com/vanderaj)) - [Brian Glas](mailto:brian.glas@owasp.org) (twitter: [@infosec"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-0x01-2021-about-owasp", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: 0x01 2021-about-owasp", "tags": ["0x01 2021-about-owasp", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# 關於 OWASP The Open Worldwide Application Security Project (OWASP) is an open community dedicated to enabling organizations to develop, purchase, and maintain applications and APIs that can be trusted"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-a00-2021-how-to-start-an-appsec-program-with-the-owasp-top-10", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: A00 2021-How to start an AppSec program with the OWASP Top 10", "tags": ["a00 2021-how to start an appsec program with the owasp top 10", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# How to start an AppSec Program with the OWASP Top 10 Previously, the OWASP Top 10 was never designed to be the basis for an AppSec program. However, it's essential to start somewhere for many organi"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-a00-2021-how-to-use-the-owasp-top-10-as-a-standard", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: A00 2021 How to use the OWASP Top 10 as a standard", "tags": ["a00 2021 how to use the owasp top 10 as a standard", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# 如何將 OWASP Top 10 2021 做為標準使用 OWASP Top 10 最主要是一個提升意識及資安認知形態的文件。但是，從 2003 年開始，這並沒有讓任何的企業或組織停止使用它當作預設的應用安全標準。如果你想要用使用 OWASP Top 10 當作程式設計或是驗證測試的一個標準，要先知道這只是一個最低限度的指標並且也只是一個開始。 使用 OWASP Top 10 作為標準的困難之"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-a00-2021-introduction", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: A00 2021 Introduction", "tags": ["a00 2021 introduction", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# OWASP Top 10 2021 介紹 歡迎來到最新版本的 OWASP Top 10！! OWASP Top 10 2021 是一個全新的名單，包含了你可以列印下來的新圖示說明，若有需要的話，你可以從我們的網頁上面下載。 在此我們想對所有貢獻了他們時間和資料的人給予一個極大的感謝。沒有你們，這一個新版本是不會出現的。**謝謝**。 ## Top 10 for 2021 有什麼新的變化？ 這次"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-a01-2021-broken-access-control", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: A01 2021-Broken Access Control", "tags": ["a01 2021-broken access control", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A01:2021 – 權限控制失效 ## 對照因素 | 可對照 CWEs 數量 | 最大發生率 | 平均發生率 |最大覆蓋範圍 | 平均覆蓋範圍 | 平均加權漏洞 | 平均加權影響 | 出現次數 | 所有相關 CVEs 數量 | |:-------------:|:--------------------:|:--------------------:|:--------------:|:--"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-a02-2021-cryptographic-failures", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: A02 2021-Cryptographic Failures", "tags": ["a02 2021-cryptographic failures", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A02:2021 – 加密機制失效 ## 弱點因素 | 可對照 CWEs 數量 | 最大發生率 | 平均發生率 |最大覆蓋範圍 | 平均覆蓋範圍 | 平均加權漏洞 | 平均加權影響 | 出現次數 | 所有相關 CVEs 數量 | |:-------------:|:--------------------:|:--------------------:|:--------------:|:--"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-a03-2021-injection", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: A03 2021-Injection", "tags": ["a03 2021-injection", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A03:2021 – 注入式攻擊 ## 對照因素 | 可對照 CWEs 數量 | 最大發生率 | 平均發生率 | 最大覆蓋範圍 | 平均覆蓋範圍 | 平均加權弱點 | 平均加權影響 | 出現次數 | 所有有關 CVEs 數量| |:-------------:|:-----------