"owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A08:2021 – Software and Data Integrity Failures ## Factors # 弱點因素 | 對應的 CWEs數量 | 最大發生率 | 平均發生率 | 最大覆蓋範圍 | 平均覆蓋範圍 | 平均加權漏洞 | 平均加權影響 | 出現次數 | 相關 CVEs 總量 | |:-------------:|:--------------------:|:----"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-a09-2021-security-logging-and-monitoring-failures", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: A09 2021-Security Logging and Monitoring Failures", "tags": ["a09 2021-security logging and monitoring failures", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A09:2021 – Security Logging and Monitoring Failures ## Factors | CWEs Mapped | Max Incidence Rate | Avg Incidence Rate | Max Coverage | Avg Coverage | Avg Weighted Exploit | Avg Weighted Impact | To"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-a10-2021-server-side-request-forgery-ssrf", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: A10 2021-Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)", "tags": ["a10 2021-server-side request forgery (ssrf)", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A10:2021 – Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) ## Factors | CWEs Mapped | Max Incidence Rate | Avg Incidence Rate | Max Coverage | Avg Coverage | Avg Weighted Exploit | Avg Weighted Impact | Total Oc"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-a11-2021-next-steps", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: A11 2021-Next Steps", "tags": ["a11 2021-next steps", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# A11:2021 – 下一步 By design, the OWASP Top 10 is innately limited to the ten most significant risks. Every OWASP Top 10 has “on the cusp” risks considered at length for inclusion, but in the end, they "}, {"id": "owasp-top10-index", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: index", "tags": ["index", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# OWASP Top 10 2021 介紹 歡迎來到最新版本的 OWASP Top 10！! OWASP Top 10 2021 是一個全新的名單，包含了你可以列印下來的新圖示說明，若有需要的話，你可以從我們的網頁上面下載。 在此我們想對所有貢獻了他們時間和資料的人給予一個極大的感謝。沒有你們，這一個新版本是不會出現的。**謝謝**。 ## Top 10 for 2021 有什麼新的變化？ 這次"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-0x00-2021-introduction", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: 0x00 2021-introduction", "tags": ["0x00 2021-introduction", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# Introduction ## Welcome to the OWASP Top 10 - 2021 ![OWASP Top 10 Logo](./assets/TOP_10_logo_Final_Logo_Colour.png){:class=\"img-responsive\"} Welcome to the latest installment of the OWASP Top 10! Th"}, {"id": "owasp-top10-0x00-notice-es", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP Top 10: 0x00-notice.es", "tags": ["0x00-notice.es", "owasp", "top10"], "summary": "# Publicación Publicado el 24 de septiembre de 2021 ## Autores principales - [Andrew van der Stock](mailto:vanderaj@owasp.org) (twitter: [@vanderaj](https://x.com/vanderaj)) - [Brian Glas](mailto:bria"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x01-frontispiece", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x01 Frontispiece", "tags": ["0x01 frontispiece", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Frontispiece ## About the Standard The Application Security Verification Standard is a list of application security requirements that architects, developers, testers, security professionals, tool ve"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x02-preface", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x02 Preface", "tags": ["0x02 preface", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Preface Welcome to the Application Security Verification Standard (ASVS) Version 5.0. ## Introduction Originally launched in 2008 through a global community collaboration, the ASVS defines a compreh"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x03-what-is-the-asvs", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x03 What is the ASVS", "tags": ["0x03 what is the asvs", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# What is the ASVS? The Application Security Verification Standard (ASVS) defines security requirements for web applications and services, and it is a valuable resource for anyone aiming to design, de"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x04-assessment-and-certification", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x04 Assessment and Certification", "tags": ["0x04 assessment and certification", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Assessment and Certification ## OWASP's Stance on ASVS Certifications and Trust Marks OWASP, as a vendor-neutral nonprofit, does not certify any vendors, verifiers, or software. Any assurance, trust"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x05-for-users-of-4-0", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x05 For Users Of 4.0", "tags": ["0x05 for users of 4.0", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Changes Compared to v4.x ## Introduction Users familiar with version 4.x of the standard may find it helpful to review the key changes introduced in version 5.0, including updates in content, scope,"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x10-v1-encoding-and-sanitization", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x10 V1 Encoding and Sanitization", "tags": ["0x10 v1 encoding and sanitization", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V1 Encoding and Sanitization ## Control Objective This chapter addresses the most common web application security weaknesses related to the unsafe processing of untrusted data. Such weaknesses can r"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x11-v2-validation-and-business-logic", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x11 V2 Validation and Business Logic", "tags": ["0x11 v2 validation and business logic", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V2 Validation and Business Logic ## Control Objective This chapter aims to ensure that a verified application meets the following high-level goals: * Input received by the application matches busine"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x12-v3-web-frontend-security", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x12 V3 Web Frontend Security", "tags": ["0x12 v3 web frontend security", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V3 Web Frontend Security ## Control Objective This chapter focuses on requirements designed to protect against attacks executed via a web frontend. These requirements do not apply to machine-to-mach"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x13-v4-api-and-web-service", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x13 V4 API and Web Service", "tags": ["0x13 v4 api and web service", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V4 API and Web Service ## Control Objective Several considerations apply specifically to applications that expose APIs for use by web browsers or other consumers (commonly using JSON, XML, or GraphQ"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x14-v5-file-handling", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x14 V5 File Handling", "tags": ["0x14 v5 file handling", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V5 File Handling ## Control Objective The use of files can present a variety of risks to the application, including denial of service, unauthorized access, and storage exhaustion. This chapter inclu"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x15-v6-authentication", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x15 V6 Authentication", "tags": ["0x15 v6 authentication", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V6 Authentication ## Control Objective Authentication is the process of establishing or confirming the authenticity of an individual or device. It involves verifying claims made by a person or about"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x16-v7-session-management", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x16 V7 Session Management", "tags": ["0x16 v7 session management", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V7 Session Management ## Control Objective Session management mechanisms allow applications to correlate user and device interactions over time, even when using stateless communication protocols (su"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x17-v8-authorization", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x17 V8 Authorization", "tags": ["0x17 v8 authorization", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V8 Authorization ## Control Objective Authorization ensures that access is granted only to permitted consumers (users, servers, and other clients). To enforce the Principle of Least Privilege (POLP)"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x18-v9-self-contained-tokens", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x18 V9 Self contained Tokens", "tags": ["0x18 v9 self contained tokens", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V9 Self-contained Tokens ## Control Objective The concept of a self-contained token is mentioned in the original RFC 6749 OAuth 2.0 from 2012. It refers to a token containing data or claims on which"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x19-v10-oauth-and-oidc", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x19 V10 OAuth and OIDC", "tags": ["0x19 v10 oauth and oidc", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V10 OAuth and OIDC ## Control Objective OAuth2 (referred to as OAuth in this chapter) is an industry-standard framework for delegated authorization. For example, using OAuth, a client application ca"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x20-v11-cryptography", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x20 V11 Cryptography", "tags": ["0x20 v11 cryptography", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V11 Cryptography ## Control Objective The objective of this chapter is to define best practices for the general use of cryptography, as well as to instill a fundamental understanding of cryptographi"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x21-v12-secure-communication", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x21 V12 Secure Communication", "tags": ["0x21 v12 secure communication", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V12 Secure Communication ## Control Objective This chapter includes requirements related to the specific mechanisms that should be in place to protect data in transit, both between an end-user clien"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x22-v13-configuration", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x22 V13 Configuration", "tags": ["0x22 v13 configuration", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V13 Configuration ## Control Objective The application's default configuration must be secure for use on the Internet. This chapter provides guidance on the various configurations necessary to achie"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x23-v14-data-protection", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x23 V14 Data Protection", "tags": ["0x23 v14 data protection", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V14 Data Protection ## Control Objective Applications cannot account for all usage patterns and user behaviors, and should therefore implement controls to limit unauthorized access to sensitive data"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x24-v15-secure-coding-and-architecture", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x24 V15 Secure Coding and Architecture", "tags": ["0x24 v15 secure coding and architecture", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V15 Secure Coding and Architecture ## Control Objective Many ASVS requirements either relate to a particular area of security, such as authentication or authorization, or pertain to a particular typ"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x25-v16-security-logging-and-error-handling", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x25 V16 Security Logging and Error Handling", "tags": ["0x25 v16 security logging and error handling", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V16 Security Logging and Error Handling ## Control Objective Security logs are distinct from error or performance logs and are used to record security-relevant events such as authentication decision"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x26-v17-webrtc", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x26 V17 WebRTC", "tags": ["0x26 v17 webrtc", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V17 WebRTC ## Control Objective Web Real-Time Communication (WebRTC) enables real-time voice, video, and data exchange in modern applications. As adoption increases, securing WebRTC infrastructure b"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs-0x90-appendix-a-glossary", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS: 0x90 Appendix A Glossary", "tags": ["0x90 appendix a glossary", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary":