01 Frontispiece", "tags": ["0x01 frontispiece", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Frontispiece ## About the Standard The Application Security Verification Standard is a list of application security requirements or tests that can be used by architects, developers, testers, securit"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x02-preface", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x02 Preface", "tags": ["0x02 preface", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Preface Welcome to the Application Security Verification Standard (ASVS) version 4.0. The ASVS is a community-driven effort to establish a framework of security requirements and controls that focus "}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x03-using-asvs", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x03 Using ASVS", "tags": ["0x03 using asvs", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Using the ASVS ASVS has two main goals: * to help organizations develop and maintain secure applications. * to allow security service vendors, security tools vendors, and consumers to align their re"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x04-assessment-and-certification", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x04 Assessment and Certification", "tags": ["0x04 assessment and certification", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# Assessment and Certification ## OWASP's Stance on ASVS Certifications and Trust Marks OWASP, as a vendor-neutral not-for-profit organization, does not currently certify any vendors, verifiers or sof"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x10-v1-architecture", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x10 V1 Architecture", "tags": ["0x10 v1 architecture", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V1 Architecture, Design and Threat Modeling ## Control Objective Security architecture has almost become a lost art in many organizations. The days of the enterprise architect have passed in the age"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x11-v2-authentication", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x11 V2 Authentication", "tags": ["0x11 v2 authentication", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V2 Authentication ## Control Objective Authentication is the act of establishing, or confirming, someone (or something) as authentic and that claims made by a person or about a device are correct, r"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x12-v3-session-management", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x12 V3 Session management", "tags": ["0x12 v3 session management", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V3 Session Management ## Control Objective One of the core components of any web-based application or stateful API is the mechanism by which it controls and maintains the state for a user or device "}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x12-v4-access-control", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x12 V4 Access Control", "tags": ["0x12 v4 access control", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V4 Access Control ## Control Objective Authorization is the concept of allowing access to resources only to those permitted to use them. Ensure that a verified application satisfies the following hi"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x13-v5-validation-sanitization-encoding", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x13 V5 Validation Sanitization Encoding", "tags": ["0x13 v5 validation sanitization encoding", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V5 Validation, Sanitization and Encoding ## Control Objective The most common web application security weakness is the failure to properly validate input coming from the client or the environment be"}, {"id": "owasp-asvs4-0x14-v6-cryptography", "source": "owasp", "title": "OWASP ASVS 4.0: 0x14 V6 Cryptography", "tags": ["0x14 v6 cryptography", "asvs", "owasp", "standard", "verification"], "summary": "# V6 Stored Cryptography ## Control Objective Ensure that a verified application satisfies the following high level requirements: * All cryptographic 