iguration Discovery\n- T1573.002 Asymmetric Cryptography\n- T1205 Traffic Signaling\n- T1040 Network Sniffing\n- T1059.004 Unix Shell\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1173": "# S1173 PowerExchange\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1173\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1173\n\n[PowerExchange](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1173) is a PowerShell backdoor that has been used by [OilRig](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0049) since at least 2023 including against government targets in the Middle East.(Citation: Symantec Crambus OCT 2023)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1071.003 Mail Protocols\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1226": "# S1226 BOOKWORM\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1226\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1226\n\n[BOOKWORM](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1226) is a modular trojan known to be leveraged by [Mustang Panda](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0129) and was first observed utilized in 2015.  [BOOKWORM](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1226) was later updated in late 2021 and the fall of 2022 to launch shellcode represented as UUID parameters. (Citation: Broadcom)(Citation: Unit42 Bookworm Nov2015)(Citation: Palo Alto Networks, Unit 42)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1553.002 Code Signing\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1112 Modify Registry\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1564.003 Hidden Window\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1036.004 Masquerade Task or Service\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- T1070.006 Timestomp\n- T1001.003 Protocol or Service Impersonation\n- T1115 Clipboard Data\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0537": "# S0537 HyperStack\n\n**