6 HTML Smuggling\n- T1187 Forced Authentication\n- T1036 Masquerading\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9022": "# S9022 MirrorStealer\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9022\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9022\n\n[MirrorStealer](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9022) is a credential stealer that has been used by [MirrorFace](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1054) since at least 2022 to steal credentials from various applications, including browsers and email clients. [MirrorStealer](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9022) has been delivered directly into system memory via commands issued by [LODEINFO](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9020).(Citation: ESET MirrorFace DEC 2022)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1555 Credentials from Password Stores\n- T1552.006 Group Policy Preferences\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n- T1555.003 Credentials from Web Browsers\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0058": "# S0058 SslMM\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0058\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0058\n\n[SslMM](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0058) is a full-featured backdoor used by [Naikon](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0019) that has multiple variants. (Citation: Baumgartner Naikon 2015)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1008 Fallback Channels\n- T1547.009 Shortcut Modification\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1134 Access Token Manipulation\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1685 Disable or Modify Tools\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1238": "# S1238 STATICPLUGIN\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1238\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1238\n\n[STATICPLUGIN](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1238) is a downloader known to be leveraged by [Mustang Panda](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0129) and was first observed utilized in 2025.  [STATICPLUGIN](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1238) has utilized a valid certificate in order to bypass endpoint security protections.  [STATICPLUGIN](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1238) masqueraded as legitimate software installer by using a custom TForm.  [STATICPLUGIN](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1238) has been leveraged to deploy a loader that facilitates follow on malware.(Citation: Google Threat Intelligence Group MUSTANG PANDA PLUGX August 2025)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1553.002 Code Signing\n- T1036.008 Masquerade File Type\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1204.002 Malicious File\n- T1559.001 Component Object Model\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1152": "# S1152 IMAPLoader\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1152\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1152\n\n[IMAPLoader](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1152) is a .NET-based loader malware exclusively associated with [CURIUM](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1012) operations since at least 2022. [IMAPLoader](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1152) leverages email protocols for command and control and payload delivery.(Citation: PWC Yellow Liderc 2023)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1543 Create or Modify System Process\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1047 Windows Management Instrumentation\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1564.003 Hidden Window\n- T1574.014 AppDomainManager\n- T1071.003 Mail Protocols\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1053.005 Scheduled Task\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0342": "# S0342 GreyEnergy\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0342\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0342\n\n[GreyEnergy](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0342) is a backdoor written in C and compiled in Visual Studio. [GreyEnergy](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0342) shares similarities with the [BlackEnergy](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0089) malware and is thought to be the successor of it.(Citation: ESET GreyEnergy Oct 2018)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1090.003 Multi-hop Proxy\n- T1218.011 Rundll32\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1553.002 Code Signing\n- T1007 System Service Discovery\n- T1573.002 Asymmetric Cryptography\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1055.002 Portable Executable Injection\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1112 Modify Registry\n- T1027.002 Software Packing\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1003.001 LSASS Memory\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1198": "# S1198 Gomir\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1198\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1198\n\nGomir is a Linux backdoor variant of the Go-based malware [GoBear](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1197), uniquely assoicated with [Kimsuky](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0094) operations.(Citation: Symantec Troll Stealer 2024)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1573 Encrypted Channel\n- T1543.002 Systemd Service\n- T1018 Remote System Discovery\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n- T1053.003 Cron\n- T1059.004 Unix Shell\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1090.001 Internal Proxy\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1069.001 Local Groups\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1573.002 Asymmetric Cryptography\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0456": "# S0456 Aria-body\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0456\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0456\n\n[Aria-body](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0456) is a custom backdoor that has been used by [Naikon](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0019) since approximately 2017.(Citation: CheckPoint Naikon May 2020)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1095 Non-Application Layer Protocol\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1568.002 Domain Generation Algorithms\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Informati