22.(Citation: Cybereason PowerLess February 2022)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1217 Browser Information Discovery\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1573 Encrypted Channel\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n- T1560 Archive Collected Data\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1028": "# S1028 Action RAT\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1028\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1028\n\n[Action RAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1028) is a  remote access tool written in Delphi that has been used by [SideCopy](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1008) since at least December 2021 against Indian and Afghani government personnel.(Citation: MalwareBytes SideCopy Dec 2021)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1047 Windows Management Instrumentation\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0473": "# S0473 Avenger\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0473\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0473\n\n[Avenger](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0473) is a downloader that has been used by [BRONZE BUTLER](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0060) since at least 2019.(Citation: Trend Micro Tick November 2019)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1055 Process Injection\n- T1027.003 Steganography\n- T1680 Local Storage Discovery\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1158": "# S1158 DUSTPAN\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1158\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1158\n\n[DUSTPAN](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1158) is an in-memory dropper written in C/C++ used by [APT41](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0096) since 2021 that decrypts and executes an embedded payload.(Citation: Google Cloud APT41 2024)(Citation: Google Cloud APT41 2022)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1055.002 Portable Executable Injection\n- T1027.009 Embedded Payloads\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0113": "# S0113 Prikormka\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0113\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0113\n\n[Prikormka](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0113) is a malware family used in a campaign known as Operation Groundbait. It has predominantly been observed in Ukraine and was used as early as 2008. (Citation: ESET Operation Groundbait)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1218.011 Rundll32\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1120 Peripheral Device Discovery\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1555.003 Credentials from Web Browsers\n- T1555 Credentials from Password Stores\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1025 Data from Removable Media\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1560 Archive Collected Data\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1228": "# S1228 PUBLOAD\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1228\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1228\n\n[PUBLOAD](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1228) is a stager malware that has been observed installing itself in existing directories such as `C:\\Users\\Public` or creating new directories to stage the malware and its components.(Citation: 2022 November_TrendMicro_Earth Preta_Toneshell_Pubload)  [PUBLOAD](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1228) malware collects details of the victim host, establishes persistence, encrypts victim details using RC4 and communicates victim details back to C2.  [PUBLOAD](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1228) malware has previously been leveraged by China-affiliated actors identified as [Mustang Panda](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0129).   [PUBLOAD](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1228) is also known as “NoFive” and some public reporting identifies the loader component as [CLAIMLOADER](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1236).(Citation: 2025_IBM_PUBLOAD_TONESHELL_HIUPAN_CLAIMLOADER_MUSTANG PANDA)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n- T1553.002 Code Signing\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1614.001 System Language Discovery\n- T1001.003 Protocol or Service Impersonation\n- T1053.005 Scheduled Task\n- T1622 Debugger Evasion\n- T1027.015 Compression\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1071.002 File Transfer Protocols\n- T1016.002 Wi-Fi Discovery\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1480.001 Environmental Keying\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1560.001 Archive via Utility\n- T1680 Local Storage Discovery\n- T1518 Software Discovery\n- T1012 Query Registry\n- T1205 Traffic Signaling\n- T1016.001 Internet Connection Discovery\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1007 System Service Discovery\n- T1124 System Time Discovery\n- T1049 System Network Connections Discovery\n- T1047 Windows Management Instrumentation\n- T1048.003 Exfiltration Over Unencrypted Non-C2 Protocol\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9001": "# S9001 SystemBC\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9001\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9001\n\n[SystemBC](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9001) is a malware family offered as a malware-as-a-service (MaaS) that is used to establish command and control and facilitate follow-on activity, including ransomware deployment.[SystemBC](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9001) executes a variety of tasks including setting up SOCKS5 proxies, maintaining persistence, ingesting malicious files, and handing C2 communication. [SystemBC](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9001) was first detected in 2018, and has been used by [Wizard Spider](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0102) since at least 2020, and by [FIN7](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0046) since at least 2022.(Citation: TrumanKroll_SYSTEMBCServer_Jan2024)(Citation: SophosGnGal_SystemBC_Dec2020)(Citation: BlackBasta)(Citation: AhnLab_SystemBC_Apr2022)(Citation: Lumen_SystemBC_Sept2025)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1053.005 Scheduled Task\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1087.001 Local Account\n- T1124 System Time Discovery\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1001 Data Obfuscation\n- T1071.004 DNS\n- T1571 Non-Standard Port\n- T1564.003 Hidden Window\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1090.003 Multi-hop Proxy\n- T1480 Execution Guardrails\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1620 Reflective Code Loading\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1678 Delay Execution\n- T1095 Non-Application Layer Protocol\n- T1059.005 Visual Basic\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1138": "# S1138 Gootloader\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1138\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1138\n\n[Gootloader](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1138) is a Javascript-based infection framework that has been used since at least 2020 as a delivery method for the Gootkit banking trojan, [Cobalt Strike](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0154), [REvil](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0496), and others. [Gootloader](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1138) operates on an \"Initial Access as a Service\" model and has leveraged [SEO Poisoning](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1608/006) to provide access to entities in multiple sectors worldwide including financial, military, automotive, pharmaceutical, and energy.(Citation: Sophos Gootloader)(Citation: SentinelOne Gootloader June 2021)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1614 System Location Discovery\n- T1584.001 Domains\n- T1069.002 Domain Groups\n- T1584.006 Web Services\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n- T1497.003 Time Based Checks\n- T1614.001 System Language Discovery\n- T1204.001 Malicious Link\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1059.007 JavaScript\n- T1055.002 Portable Executable Injection\n- T1055.012 Process Hollowing\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1031": "# S1031 PingPull\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1031\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1031\n\n[PingPull](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1031) is a remote access Trojan (RAT) written in Visual C++ that has been used by [GALLIUM](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0093) since at least June 2022. [PingPull](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1031) has been used to target telecommunications companies, financial institutions, and government entities in Afghanistan, Australia, Belgium, Cambodia, Malaysia, Mozambique, the Philippines, Russia, and Vietnam.(Citation: Unit 42 PingPull Jun 2022)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1571 Non-Standard Port\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1036.004 Masquerade Task or Service\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1070.006 Timestomp\n- T1095 Non-Application Layer Protocol\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0514": "# S0514 WellMess\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0514\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0514\n\n[WellMess](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0514) is lightweight malware family with variants written in .NET and Golang that has been in use since at least 2018 by [APT29](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0016).(Citation: CISA WellMess July 2020)(Citation: PWC WellMess July 2020)(Citation: NCSC APT29 July 2020)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1071.004 DNS\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1573.002 Asymmetric Cryptography\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1069.002 Domain Groups\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1001.001 Junk Data\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0497": "# S0497 Dacls\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0497\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0497\n\n[Dacls](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0497) is a multi-platform remote access tool used by [Lazarus Group](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0032) since at least December 2019.(Citation: TrendMicro macOS Dacls May 2020)(Citation: SentinelOne Lazarus macOS July 2020)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1543.001 Launch Agent\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1543.004 Launch Daemon\n- T1564.001 Hidden Files and Directories\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1036 Masquerading\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0547": "# S0547 DropBook\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0547\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0547\n\n[DropBook](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0547) is a Python-based backdoor compiled with PyInstaller.(Citation: Cybereason Molerats Dec 2020)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1059.006 Python\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1102 Web Service\n- T1567 Exfiltration Over Web Service\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1614.001 System Language Discovery\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1065": "# S1065 Woody RAT\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1065\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1065\n\n[Woody RAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1065) is a remote access trojan (RAT) that has been used since at least August 2021 against Russian organizations.(Citation: MalwareBytes WoodyRAT Aug 2022)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1055.012 Process Hollowing\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1680 Local Storage Discovery\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n- T1087 Account Discovery\n- T1005 Data from