3 Archive via Custom Method\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1497 Virtualization/Sandbox Evasion\n- T1218.011 Rundll32\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0064": "# S0064 ELMER\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0064\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0064\n\n[ELMER](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0064) is a non-persistent, proxy-aware HTTP backdoor written in Delphi that has been used by [APT16](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0023). (Citation: FireEye EPS Awakens Part 2)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1237": "# S1237 CANONSTAGER\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1237\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1237\n\n[CANONSTAGER](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1237) is a loader known to be leveraged by [Mustang Panda](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0129) and was first observed utilized in 2025.  [Mustang Panda](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0129) utilizes DLL side-loading to execute within the victim environment prior to delivering a follow-on malicious encrypted payload.  [CANONSTAGER](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1237) leverages Thread Local Storage (TLS) and Native Windows APIs within the victim environment to elude detections. [CANONSTAGER](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1237) also hides its code utilizing window procedures and message queues.(Citation: Google Threat Intelligence Group MUSTANG PANDA PLUGX August 2025)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1027.007 Dynamic API Resolution\n- T1055.005 Thread Local Storage\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1564.003 Hidden Window\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0518": "# S0518 PolyglotDuke\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0518\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0518\n\n[PolyglotDuke](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0518) is a downloader that has been used by [APT29](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0016) since at least 2013. [PolyglotDuke](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0518) has been used to drop [MiniDuke](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0051).(Citation: ESET Dukes October 2019)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1112 Modify Registry\n- T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- T1027.011 Fileless Storage\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1218.011 Rundll32\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1102.001 Dead Drop Resolver\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1027.003 Steganography\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1249": "# S1249 HexEval Loader\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1249\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1249\n\n[HexEval Loader](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1249) is a hex-encoded loader that collects host data, decodes follow-on scripts and acts as a downloader for the [BeaverTail](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1246) malware.  [HexEval Loader](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1249) was first reported in April 2025.  [HexEval Loader](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1249) has previously been leveraged by North Korea-affiliated threat actors identified as [Contagious Interview](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1052).  [HexEval Loader](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1249) has been delivered to victims through code repository sites utilizing typosquatting naming conventions of various npm packages.(Citation: Socket Contagious Interview NPM April 2025)(Citation: Socket BeaverTail XORIndex HexEval Contagious Interview July 2025)(Citation: Socket HexEval BeaverTail Contagious Interview June 2025)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1059.007 JavaScript\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1614 System Location Discovery\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0221": "# S0221 Umbreon\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0221\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0221\n\nA Linux rootkit that provides backdoor access and hides from defenders.\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1014 Rootkit\n- T1205 Traffic Signaling\n- T1095 Non-Application Layer Protocol\n- T1078.003 Local Accounts\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1029": "# S1029 AuTo Stealer\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1029\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1029\n\n[AuTo Stealer](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1029) is malware written in C++ has been used by [SideCopy](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1008) since at least December 2021 to target government agencies and personnel in India and Afghanistan.(Citation: MalwareBytes SideCopy Dec 2021)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1095 Non-Application Layer Protocol\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1178": "# S1178 ShrinkLocker\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1178\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1178\n\n[ShrinkLocker](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1178) is a VBS-based malicious script that leverages the legitimate Bitlocker application to encrypt files on victim systems for ransom. [ShrinkLocker](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1178) functions by using Bitlocker to encrypt files, then renames impacted drives to the adversary’s contact email address to facilitate communication for the ransom payment.(Citation: Kaspersky ShrinkLocker 2024)(Citation: Splunk ShrinkLocker 2024)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1124 System Time Discovery\n- T1491.001 Internal Defacement\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1059.005 Visual Basic\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n- T1112 Modify Registry\n- T1685.005 Clear Windows Event Logs\n- T1047 Windows Management Instrumentation\n- T1102 Web Service\n- T1486 Data Encrypted for Impact\n- T1561.002 Disk Structure Wipe\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1529 System Shutdown/Reboot\n- T1685 Disable or Modify Tools\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1686 Disable or Modify System Firewall\n- T1480 Execution Guardrails\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1485 Data Destruction\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0601": "# S0601 Hildegard\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0601\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0601\n\n[Hildegard](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0601) is malware that targets misconfigured kubelets for initial access and runs cryptocurrency miner operations. The malware was first observed in January 2021. The TeamTNT activity group is believed to be behind [Hildegard](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0601). (Citation: Unit 42 Hildegard Malware)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1071 Application Layer Protocol\n- T1552.004 Private Keys\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1609 Container Administration Command\n- T1613 Container and Resource Discovery\n- T1574.006 Dynamic Linker Hijacking\n- T1046 Network Service Discovery\n- T1133 External Remote Services\n- T1552.001 Credentials In Files\n- T1027.002 Software Packing\n- T1036.004 Masquerade Task or Service\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1102 Web Service\n- T1685 Disable or Modify Tools\n- T1014 Rootkit\n- T1070.003 Clear Command History\n- T1219 Remote Access Tools\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1496.001 Compute Hijacking\n- T1136.001 Local Account\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1552.005 Cloud Instance Metadata API\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1543.002 Systemd Service\n- T1611 Escape to Host\n- T1068 Exploitation for Privilege Escalation\n- T1059.004 Unix Shell\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0092": "# S0092 Agent.btz\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0092\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0092\n\n[Agent.btz](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0092) is a worm that primarily spreads itself via removable devices such as USB drives. It reportedly infected U.S. military networks in 2008. (Citation: Securelist Agent.btz)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1091 Replication Through Removable Media\n- T1052.001 Exfiltration over USB\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1560.003 Archive via Custom Method\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0218": "# S0218 SLOWDRIFT\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0218\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0218\n\n[SLOWDRIFT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0218) is a backdoor used by [APT37](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0067) against academic and strategic victims in South Korea. (Citation: FireEye APT37 Feb 2018)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1102.002 Bidirectional Communication\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0217": "# S0217 SHUTTERSPEED\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0217\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0217\n\n[SHUTTERSPEED](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0217) is a backdoor used by [APT37](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0067). (Citation: FireEye APT37 Feb 2018)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0615": "# S0615 SombRAT\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0615\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0615\n\n[SombRAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0615) is a modular backdoor written in C++ that has been used since at least 2019 to download and execute malicious payloads, including [FIVEHANDS](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0618) ransomware.(Citation: BlackBerry CostaRicto November 2020)(Citation: FireEye FiveHands April 2021)(Citation: CISA AR21-126A FIVEHANDS May 2021)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1573.002 Asymmetric Cryptography\n- T1124 System Time Discovery\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1090 Proxy\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1095 Non-Application Layer Protocol\n- T1564.010 Process Argument Spoofing\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1560.003 Archive via Custom Method\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1071.004 DNS\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n- T1568.002 Domain Generation Algorithms\n- T1007 System Service Discovery\n- T1055.001 Dynamic-link Library Injection\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1036 Masquerading\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1170": "# S1170 ODAgent\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1170\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1170\n\n[ODAgent](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1170) is a C#/.NET downloader that has been used by [OilRig](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0049) since at least 2022 including against target organizations in Israel to download and execute payloads and to exfiltrate staged files.(Citation: ESET OilRig Downloaders DEC 2023)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1567.002 Exfiltration to Cloud Storage\n- T1102.002 Bidirectional Communication\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1181": "# S1181 BlackByte 2.0 Ransomware\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1181\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1181\n\n[BlackByte 2.0 Ransomware](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1181) is a replacement for [BlackByte Ransomware](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1180). Unlike [BlackByte Ransomware](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1180), [BlackByte 2.0 Ransomware](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1181) does not have a common key for victim decryption. [BlackByte 2.0 Ransomware](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1181) remains uniquely associated with [BlackByte](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1043) operations.(Citation: Microsoft BlackByte 2023)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1070.006 Timestomp\n- T1112 Modify Registry\n- T1486 Data Encrypted for Impact\n- T1490 Inhibit System Recovery\n- T1068 Exploitation for Privilege Escalation\n- T1135 Network Share Discovery\n- T1489 Service Stop\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1569.002 Service Execution\n- T1055 Process Injection\n- T1686.003 Windows Host Firewall\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0383": "# S0383 FlawedGrace\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0383\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0383\n\n[FlawedGrace](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0383) is a fully featured remote access tool (RAT) written in C++ that was first observed in late 2017.(Citation: Proofpoint TA505 Jan 2019)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0036": "# S0036 FLASHFLOOD\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0036\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0036\n\n[FLASHFLOOD](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0036) is malware developed by [APT30](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0013) that allows propagation and exfiltration of data over removable devices. [APT30](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0013) may use this capability to exfiltrate data across air-gaps. (Citation: FireEye APT30)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1025 Data from Removable Media\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n- T1560.003 Archive via Custom Method\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0381": "# S0381 FlawedAmmyy\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0381\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0381\n\n[FlawedAmmyy](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0381) is a remote access tool (RAT) that was first seen in early 2016. The code for [FlawedAmmyy](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0381) was based on leaked source code for a version of Ammyy Admin, a remote access software.(Citation: Proofpoint TA505 Mar 2018)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1056.001 Keylogging\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1047 Windows Management Instrumentation\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n- T1218.011 Rundll32\n- T1120 Peripheral Device Discovery\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1056 Input Capture\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1115 Clipboard Data\n- T1001 Data Obfuscation\n- T1218.007 Msiexec\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1069.001 Local Groups\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1086": "# S1086 Snip3\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1086\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1086\n\n[Snip3](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1086) is a sophisticated crypter-as-a-service that has been used since at least 2021 to obfuscate and load numerous strains of malware including [AsyncRAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1087), [Revenge RAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0379), [Agent Tesla](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0331), and [NETWIRE](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0198).(Citation: Morphisec Snip3 May 2021)(Citation: Telefonica Snip3 December 2021)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1102 Web Service\n- T1059.005 Visual Basic\n- T1055.012 Process Hollowing\n- T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1204.002 Malicious File\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1204.001 Malicious Link\n- T1566.001 Spearphishing Attachment\n- T1497.003 Time Based Checks\n- T1047 Windows Management Instrumentation\n- T1104 Multi-Stage Channels\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1566.002 Spearphishing Link\n- T1189 Drive-by Compromise\n- T1497.001 System Checks\n- T1564.003 Hidden Window\n- T1027.001 Binary Padding\n- T1059.001 PowerShell\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0628": "# S0628 FYAnti\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0628\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0628\n\n[FYAnti](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0628) is a loader that has been used by [menuPass](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0045) since at least 2020, including to deploy [QuasarRAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0262).(Citation: Securelist APT10 March 2021)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1027.002 Software Packing\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0433": "# S0433 Rifdoor\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0433\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0433\n\n[Rifdoor](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0433) is a remote access trojan (RAT) that shares numerous code similarities with [HotCroissant](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0431).(Citation: Carbon Black HotCroissant April 2020)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1027.001 Binary Padding\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n- T1566.001 Spearphishing Attachment\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1204.002 Malicious File\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1049": "# S1049 SUGARUSH\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1049\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1049\n\n[SUGARUSH](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1049) is a small custom backdoor that can establish a reverse shell over TCP to a hard coded C2 address. [SUGARUSH](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1049) was first identified during analysis of UNC3890's [C0010](https://attack.mitre.org/campaigns/C0010) campaign targeting Israeli companies, which began in late 2020.(Citation: Mandiant UNC3890 Aug 2022)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1680 Local Storage Discovery\n- T1571 Non-Standard Port\n- T1016.001 Internet Connection Discovery\n- T1543.003 Windows Service\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1095 Non-Application Layer Protocol\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1101": "# S1101 LoFiSe\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1101\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1101\n\n[LoFiSe](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1101) has been used by [ToddyCat](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1022) since at least 2023 to identify and collect files of interest on targeted systems.(Citation: Kaspersky ToddyCat Check Logs October 2023)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1560 Archive Collected Data\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1119 Automated Collection\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0376": "# S0376 HOPLIGHT\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0376\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0376\n\n[HOPLIGHT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0376) is a backdoor Trojan that has reportedly been used by the North Korean government.(Citation: US-CERT HOPLIGHT Apr 2019)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1652 Device Driver Discovery\n- T1112 Modify Registry\n- T1008 Fallback Channels\n- T1012 Query Registry\n- T1090 Proxy\n- T1571 Non-Standard Port\n- T1550.002 Pass the Hash\n- T1686 Disable or Modify System Firewall\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1003.002 Security Account Manager\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1546.003 Windows Management Instrumentation Event Subscription\n- T1569.002 Service Execution\n- T1680 Local Storage Discovery\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1047 Windows Management Instrumentation\n- T1124 System Time Discovery\n- T1055 Process Injection\n", "mitre-attack-software-s1153": "# S1153 Cuckoo Stealer\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S1153\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1153\n\n[Cuckoo Stealer](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1153) is a macOS malware with characteristics of spyware and an infostealer that has been in use since at least 2024. [Cuckoo Stealer](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1153) is a universal Mach-O binary that can run on Intel or ARM-based Macs and has been spread through trojanized versions of various potentially unwanted programs or PUP's such as converters, cleaners, and uninstallers.(Citation: Kandji Cuckoo April 2024)(Citation: SentinelOne Cuckoo Stealer May 2024)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1564.001 Hidden Files and Directories\n- T1614.001 System Language Discovery\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1614 System Location Discovery\n- T1569.001 Launchctl\n- T1518 Software Discovery\n- T1647 Plist File Modification\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1027.008 Stripped Payloads\n- T1140 De