sed modular backdoor that has been used by China-nexus cyber espionage actors including [UNC3886](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1048) and [APT41](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0096).(Citation: Google Cloud Mandiant UNC3886 2024)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1102 Web Service\n- T1102.001 Dead Drop Resolver\n- T1095 Non-Application Layer Protocol\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0284": "# S0284 More_eggs\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0284\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0284\n\n[More_eggs](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0284) is a JScript backdoor used by [Cobalt Group](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0080) and [FIN6](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0037). Its name was given based on the variable \"More_eggs\" being present in its code. There are at least two different versions of the backdoor being used, version 2.0 and version 4.4. (Citation: Talos Cobalt Group July 2018)(Citation: Security Intelligence More Eggs Aug 2019)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1016.001 Internet Connection Discovery\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1573.001 Symmetric Cryptography\n- T1059.003 Windows Command Shell\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n- T1553.002 Code Signing\n- T1218.010 Regsvr32\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n", "mitre-attack-software-s0663": "# S0663 SysUpdate\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S0663\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0663\n\n[SysUpdate](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0663) is a backdoor written in C++ that has been used by [Threat Group-3390](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0027) since at least