ted wiper component and can use decentralized C2 infrastructure implemented via an Internet Computer Protocol (ICP) blockchain canister.(Citation: Aikido TeamPCP Telnyx MAR 2026)(Citation: Palo Alto TeamPCP MAR 2026)(Citation: Aikido CanisterWorm MAR 2026)(Citation: Aikido TeamPCP Trivy MAR 2026)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1059.006 Python\n- T1613 Container and Resource Discovery\n- T1528 Steal Application Access Token\n- T1124 System Time Discovery\n- T1569.003 Systemctl\n- T1036.004 Masquerade Task or Service\n- T1529 System Shutdown/Reboot\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1497.003 Time Based Checks\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1677 Poisoned Pipeline Execution\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1102.001 Dead Drop Resolver\n- T1609 Container Administration Command\n- T1480 Execution Guardrails\n- T1059.004 Unix Shell\n- T1053.006 Systemd Timers\n- T1543 Create or Modify System Process\n- T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery\n- T1552.004 Private Keys\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1550.001 Application Access Token\n- T1027.009 Embedded Payloads\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1195.001 Compromise Software Dependencies and Development Tools\n- T1059.007 JavaScript\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1018 Remote System Discovery\n- T1485 Data Destruction\n- T1614.001 System Language Discovery\n- T1548.003 Sudo and Sudo Caching\n- T1555.006 Cloud Secrets Management Stores\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9044": "# S9044 Kali365\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9044\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9044\n\n[Kali365](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9044) is a Phishing-as-a-Service (PHaaS) kit first observed in April 2026 that generates victim-targeted lures across multiple operating systems to induce users into copying and pasting actor-controlled commands for local execution.(Citation: Artic Wolf Labs Kali365 Device Code April 2026)(Citation: FBI IC3 Alert I-052126 Kali365 May 2026)(Citation: Huntress Kali365 Device Code June 2026)(Citation: SpyCloud Kali365 June 2026)  [Kali365](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9044) incorporates on-demand device code generation and mirrors the copy-paste execution tradecraft associated with ClickFix. (Citation: Huntress Kali365 Device Code June 2026) Operators have used [Kali365](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9044) to harvest victims' OAuth tokens and session cookies through adversary-in-the-middle (AiTM) interception, enabling account takeover.(Citation: Artic Wolf Labs Kali365 Device Code April 2026)(Citation: Artic Wolf Kali365 Device Code OAuth June 2026)(Citation: FBI IC3 Alert I-052126 Kali365 May 2026)(Citation: Huntress Kali365 Device Code June 2026)(Citation: SpyCloud Kali365 June 2026)  [Kali365](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9044) PHaaS was first observed in April 2026.(Citation: Artic Wolf Labs Kali365 Device Code April 2026)  [Kali365](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9044) has also been affiliated with other branding to include Octopi365 and Freedom365.(Citation: Huntress Kali365 Device Code June 2026)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1566.002 Spearphishing Link\n- T1683.001 Written Content\n- T1102 Web Service\n- T1090 Proxy\n- T1552.001 Credentials In Files\n- T1539 Steal Web Session Cookie\n- T1528 Steal Application Access Token\n- T1557 Adversary-in-the-Middle\n- T1566.001 Spearphishing Attachment\n- T1204.001 Malicious Link\n- T1564.008 Email Hiding Rules\n- T1087.003 Email Account\n- T1550.001 Application Access Token\n- T1059.007 JavaScript\n- T1185 Browser Session Hijacking\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1204.004 Malicious Copy and Paste\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9062": "# S9062 MiniBrowse\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9062\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9062\n\n[MiniBrowse](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9062) is a custom stealer designed for the theft of credentials in browsers and passwords stores. [MiniBrowse](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9062) was first observed in late-2025.(Citation: CheckPoint_NimbusManticoreEurope_Sept2025) [MiniBrowse](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9062) has been affiliated with the cyber espionage threat group [NIMBUS MANTICORE](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1059).(Citation: CheckPoint_NimbusManticoreEurope_Sept2025)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1555.003 Credentials from Web Browsers\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1559 Inter-Process Communication\n- T1027.016 Junk Code Insertion\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1069.002 Domain Groups\n- T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information\n- T1217 Browser Information Discovery\n- T1059.007 JavaScript\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9052": "# S9052 MiniFast\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9052\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9052\n\n[MiniFast](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9052) is a custom malware designed for long-term persistence and remote code execution. [MiniFast](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9052) is a modular malware suspected of being generated using artificial intelligence (AI). [MiniFast](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9052) was first observed in early-2026 and is a modified version of the [MiniJunk](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9053) framework. [MiniFast](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9052) has been affiliated with the cyber espionage threat group [NIMBUS MANTICORE](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1059).(Citation: CheckPoint_NimbusManticore_May2026)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1553.002 Code Signing\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n- T1489 Service Stop\n- T1053.005 Scheduled Task\n- T1036.012 Browser Fingerprint\n- T1134.002 Create Process with Token\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1