(https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1059).(Citation: Mandiant_UNC1549_Nov2025)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1008 Fallback Channels\n- T1033 System Owner/User Discovery\n- T1132.001 Standard Encoding\n- T1083 File and Directory Discovery\n- T1678 Delay Execution\n- T1070.004 File Deletion\n- T1082 System Information Discovery\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1059.004 Unix Shell\n- T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9060": "# S9060 MiniBus\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9060\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9060\n\n[MiniBus](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9060) is a custom backdoor used for command execution, data discovery, gathering, and exfiltration. [MiniBus](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9060) has utilized Azure Cloud Infrastructure and unique adversary-controlled domains for command and control. [MiniBus](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9060) is an updated platform to its predecessor [MiniBike](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9059) and was first observed in August 2023. [MiniBus](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9060) has been affiliated with the cyber espionage threat group [NIMBUS MANTICORE](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1059).(Citation: Mandiant_UNC1549_Feb2024)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1105 Ingress Tool Transfer\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1057 Process Discovery\n- T1673 Virtual Machine Discovery\n- T1497.001 System Checks\n- T1518.001 Security Software Discovery\n- T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9058": "# S9058 SIGHTGRAB\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9058\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9058\n\n[SIGHTGRAB](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9058) is a Windows executable written in C that captures and stages stolen data on victim devices.(Citation: Mandiant_UNC1549_Nov2025) [SIGHTGRAB](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9058) was first observed in 2025 and has been affiliated with the cyber espionage threat group [NIMBUS MANTICORE](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1059).(Citation: Mandiant_UNC1549_Nov2025)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1106 Native API\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1119 Automated Collection\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n- T1113 Screen Capture\n- T1124 System Time Discovery\n- T1140 Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9065": "# S9065 DCSYNCER.SLICK\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9065\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9065\n\n[DCSYNCER.SLICK](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9065) is a Windows executable that is designed to gather credentials from victim devices.(Citation: Mandiant_UNC1549_Nov2025) [DCSYNCER.SLICK](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9065) was first observed in 2025 and has been affiliated with the cyber espionage threat group [NIMBUS MANTICORE](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1059).(Citation: Mandiant_UNC1549_Nov2025)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1036.005 Match Legitimate Resource Name or Location\n- T1005 Data from Local System\n- T1574.001 DLL\n- T1027.013 Encrypted/Encoded File\n- T1003.006 DCSync\n- T1074.001 Local Data Staging\n- T1027.007 Dynamic API Resolution\n", "mitre-attack-software-s9066": "# S9066 POLLBLEND\n\n**ATT&CK ID:** S9066\n**Type:** software\n**Aliases:** n/a\n**Reference:** https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9066\n\n[POLLBLEND](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9066) is a Windows tunneler written C++ that has utilized hardcoded C2 servers and leveraged hardcoded URI parameters for follow-on actions.(Citation: Mandiant_UNC1549_Nov2025) [POLLBLEND](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9066) was first observed in 2025 and has been affiliated with the cyber espionage threat group [NIMBUS MANTICORE](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G1059).(Citation: Mandiant_UNC1549_Nov2025)\n\n## Techniques used\n- T1071.001 Web Protocols\n- T1553.002 Code Signing\n- T1105 Ingress